notes: JCM 510 declared methane-air(50:50) cultivation gas blend. The two immediate
  gases are explicit in the primary recipe. The ratio basis is not specified, so 50:50
  is retained literally in identity/protocol notes without inventing mass, mole or
  volume fractions. Air is not expanded into guessed gases. This is the supplied gas
  blend, not the whole growth medium or a neat-methane synonym. Use as the cultivation
  atmosphere per JCM 510; temperature/pressure and humidity are not specified.  Raw
  source labels remain source-scoped in the decisions; no generic label is published
  as a global synonym. Quantified components use the literal preparation batch unless
  explicitly marked MG_PER_L. Component names retain source specificity without inferred
  vitamer, hydrate or stereoisomer IDs. Occurrence counts remain zero pending source-specific
  integration. No roles or downstream hold release is proposed.
